# ---------------------------------------- NOT satisfiable on mainline 7.2 (info)
# ACK-only / removed upstream / clang-only; the VINTF kernel check fails on these
# anyway, and on the version itself (newest matrix entry is 6.12.x):
#   ASHMEM, CPU_FREQ_TIMES, UID_SYS_STATS, DM_DEFAULT_KEY, DM_USER,
#   NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_QUOTA2(_LOG), NF_CT_PROTO_DCCP/UDPLITE, SCHED_DEBUG,
#   ARM64_PAN (always on now), CC_IS_CLANG/LD_IS_LLD/AS_IS_LLVM/CFI_CLANG (GCC
#   build), SND/SOUND + USB_CONFIGFS_F_MIDI (a9.config keeps sound off; turn
#   on together with an audio bring-up).
# DM_DEFAULT_KEY matters for the REAL userdata (metadata encryption): mainline
# cannot mount the stock-encrypted /data. Bring-up must use a RAM/zram /data.

# ---------------------------------------------------------- /data RAM disk
# First Android boots keep the user's userdata untouched: /data is a brd RAM
# disk (cmdline brd.rd_nr=1 brd.rd_size=3145728), formatted ext4 by fs_mgr
# ("formattable") at every boot. scripts/mainline/android/vendor/etc/fstab.hlte556n.
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM_COUNT=1
